{"author_count":3,"contributors":["Maguire, James","Albris, Kristoffer"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-731117"],"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"introduction digitally mediated mis trust","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.14324/111.9781800086142","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-731117","ids":["ku-50071cb0-56ba-4392-a666-a025c43c386f"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-2CD12F8F3171EE3F57FA60A8566F6A9D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/387034073/The_Encyclopaedia_of_Informality_Volume_3.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.14324/111.9781800086142","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Anthropology","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Anthropology, Copenhagen Center for Disaster Research","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Faculty of Social Sciences, shared expenditure, Social Data Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"James","key":"maguirepau","last":"Maguire","name":"Maguire, James","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Kristoffer Langkjær","key":"albrispau","last":"Albris","locid":"3562b196-6355-4e87-a1de-c22863765de9","name":"Albris, Kristoffer","name_org":"Albris, Kristoffer Langkjær","orcid":"0000-0002-1201-2231","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Alena","key":"ledenevapedh","last":"Ledeneva","name":"Ledeneva, Alena","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.14324/111.9781800086142","eisbn":["9781800086173"],"isbn":["9781800086166"],"pages":"105-107","place":"London","status":"p","subtitle":"A hitchhiker’s guide to informal problem-solving in human life","title":"The Global Encyclopaedia of Informality","volume":"3"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-50071cb0-56ba-4392-a666-a025c43c386f"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Introduction : digitally mediated (mis)trust","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-731117","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"It is becoming increasingly difficult to address environmental questions without considering how they overlap and intersect with digital concerns. We observe and make our understandings of environments through, for example, digital devices, spreadsheet accounting and carbon calculations. Conversely, we make the digital through the appropriation of environmental forms; crafting metals and plastics into sleek handheld devices, while powering our data use through vast quantities of energy consumption. We have brought epochal shifts into being through rhetoric, disciplines, and geological measures. Yet the ‘we’ of these statements is an unevenly distributed set of actors, whose politics is pressing. While it is evident that the anthropocene is constituted through colonial histories, what this collection foregrounds is how deeply interwoven it is with the tools, devices, and computational logics that are part of such histories. In this special issue, we bring together four anthropology and Science and Technology (STS) scholars, each of whom offers a different empirical instance of approaching digital anthropocenes. Through various modes of sensing, governing, intervening, and speculating, each article reveals a particular colonial legacy that provokes an alternate form of politics (proto, limit, civic, and pre-figurative). What is revealed in each case, we claim, is the legacy of a colonial infrastructure that whilst saturated in forms of technological inequality and injustice also affords a counter political re-imagining through digital mediations.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Maguire, James","Andersen, Astrid","Douglas-Jones, Rachel"],"cuid":["S02-097.00-822397"],"filters":{"added":"2024-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Maguire, James"],"keyword":["Anthropocene","Coloniality","Digital","Double Vision","Folds"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"introduction approaching digital anthropocene s a double vision","src":["aau","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.natcult.net/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/introduction_nc6.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-097.00-822397","ids":["aau-96f1f975-39d7-4f00-9937-c0fa5123841d","itu-5ef2369e-f96e-4ba3-8541-8b852b409fe9"],"keyword":["Anthropocene","coloniality","digital","double vision","folds"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-2-32D01DF4D22E8AEE8825E4EFFD3A0803"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://www.natcult.net/journal/issue-6/introduction/","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.natcult.net/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/introduction_nc6.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Climate IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Culture and Learning","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Culture and Learning, The Techno-Anthropology Lab","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Green Societies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"James","key":"maguirepau","last":"Maguire","locid":"2efbc294-1ce4-4148-a403-93fe6450d879","name":"Maguire, James","orcid":"0000-0001-5081-1811","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Astrid Oberborbeck","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"29717065-a01d-45cb-9f21-a056953ed9bd","name":"Andersen, Astrid Oberborbeck","orcid":"0000-0002-7811-1427","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rachel","key":"douglasjonespau","last":"Douglas-Jones","locid":"f11b0cc1-ad9f-4b12-b805-65b70e5bcd65","name":"Douglas-Jones, Rachel","orcid":"0000-0001-9562-6572","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["24361410"],"issue":"6","journal":"NatureCulture","paperid":"1","status":"p","title":"NatureCulture"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-96f1f975-39d7-4f00-9937-c0fa5123841d","itu-5ef2369e-f96e-4ba3-8541-8b852b409fe9"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Introduction. Approaching digital anthropocene(s): A Double Vision","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-097.00-822397","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Nebular-phase observations of peculiar Type Ia supernovae (SNe Ia) provide important constraints on progenitor scenarios and explosion dynamics for both these rare SNe and the more common, cosmologically useful SNe Ia. We present observations from an extensive ground- and space-based follow-up campaign to characterize SN 2022pul, a super-Chandrasekhar mass SN Ia (alternatively “03fg-like” SN), from before peak brightness to well into the nebular phase across optical to mid-infrared (MIR) wavelengths. The early rise of the light curve is atypical, exhibiting two distinct components, consistent with SN Ia ejecta interacting with dense carbon-oxygen (C/O)-rich circumstellar material (CSM). In the optical, SN 2022pul is most similar to SN 2012dn, having a low estimated peak luminosity (MB = −18.9 mag) and high photospheric velocity relative to other 03fg-like SNe. In the nebular phase, SN 2022pul adds to the increasing diversity of the 03fg-like subclass. From 168 to 336 days after peak B-band brightness, SN 2022pul exhibits asymmetric and narrow emission from [O I] λλ6300, 6364 (FWHM ≈ 2000 km s−1), strong, broad emission from [Ca II] λλ7291, 7323 (FWHM ≈ 7300 km s−1), and a rapid Fe III to Fe II ionization change. Finally, we present the first ever optical-to-MIR nebular spectrum of an 03fg-like SN Ia using data from JWST. In the MIR, strong lines of neon and argon, weak emission from stable nickel, and strong thermal dust emission (with T ≈ 500 K), combined with prominent [O I] in the optical, suggest that SN 2022pul was produced by a white dwarf merger within C/O-rich CSM.","author_count":81,"contributors":["Siebert, Matthew R.","Kwok, Lindsey A.","Johansson, Joel","Jha, Saurabh W.","Blondin, Stéphane","Dessart, Luc","Foley, Ryan J.","Hillier, D. John","Larison, Conor","Pakmor, Rüdiger","Temim, Tea","Andrews, Jennifer E.","Auchettl, Katie","Badenes, Carles","Barna, Barnabas","Bostroem, K. Azalee","Brenner Newman, Max J.","Brink, Thomas G.","Bustamante-Rosell, María José","Camacho-Neves, Yssavo","Clocchiatti, Alejandro","Coulter, David A.","Davis, Kyle W.","Deckers, Maxime","Dimitriadis, Georgios","Dong, Yize","Farah, Joseph","Filippenko, Alexei V.","Flörs, Andreas","Fox, Ori D.","Garnavich, Peter","Gonzalez, Estefania Padilla","Graur, Or","Hambsch, Franz Josef","Hosseinzadeh, Griffin","Howell, D. Andrew","Hughes, John P.","Kerzendorf, Wolfgang E.","Le Saux, Xavier K.","Maeda, Keiichi","Maguire, Kate","McCully, Curtis","Mihalenko, Cassidy","Newsome, Megan","O'Brien, John T.","Pearson, Jeniveve","Pellegrino, Craig","Pierel, Justin D.R.","Polin, Abigail","Rest, Armin","Rojas-Bravo, César","Sand, David J.","Schwab, Michaela","Shahbandeh, Melissa","Shrestha, Manisha","Strolger, Louis Gregory","Szalai, Tamás","Taggart, Kirsty","Terreran, Giacomo","Terwel, Jacco H.","Tinyanont, Samaporn","Valenti, Stefano","Vinkó, József","Wheeler, J. Craig","Yang, Yi","Zheng, Wei Kang","Ashall, Chris","DerKacy, James M.","Galbany, Lluís","Hoeflich, Peter","Hsiao, Eric","de Jaeger, Thomas","Lu, Jing","Maund, Justyn","Medler, Kyle","Morrell, Nidia","Shappee, Benjamin J.","Stritzinger, M. D.","Suntzeff, Nicholas","Tucker, Michael","Wang, Lifan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-717310"],"filters":{"added":"2024-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","America, South","Asia, East","Asia, South","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"country":["Australia","Belgium","Chile","France","Germany","Hungary","Ireland","Japan","Spain","Sweden","Thailand","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["ARC Centre of Excellence for All-Sky Astrophysics in 3 Dimension (ASTRO 3D)","All Global Affiliations","American Association of Variable Star Observers","American Museum of Natural History","Bundesdeutsche Arbeitsgemeinschaft fur Veranderliche Sterne E.V. (BAV)","California Institute of Technology","Carnegie Science","Consejo Superior de Investigaciones Científicas (CSIC)","ELKH-SZTE Stellar Astrophysics Research Group","Eotvos Lorand University","Florida State University","French National Centre for Scientific Research (CNRS)","GSI Helmholtz Centre for Heavy Ion Research","Gemini Observatory","Groupe Européen d'Observations Stellaires (GEOS)","Hungarian Academy of Sciences","Institut d 'Astrophysique de Paris","Institute of Space Studies of Catalonia","Instituto Milenio de Astrofísica","Isaac Newton Group of Telescopes","Johns Hopkins University","Kyoto University","Las Cumbres Observatory Global Telescope Network, Inc.","Liverpool John Moores University","Max Planck Institute for Astrophysics","Michigan State University","National Astronomical Research Institute of Thailand","Ohio State University","Pontificia Universidad Catolica de Chile","Princeton University","Rutgers - The State University of New Jersey, New Brunswick","Sheffield Hallam University","Sorbonne Université","Space Telescope Science Institute","Stockholm University","Texas A and M University","Trinity College Dublin","University of Arizona","University of California at Berkeley","University of California at Davis","University of California at Santa Barbara","University of California at Santa Cruz","University of Hawaii at Manoa","University of Melbourne","University of Notre Dame","University of Pittsburgh","University of Portsmouth","University of Szeged","University of Texas at Austin","Vereniging voor Sterrenkunde (VVS)","Virginia Polytechnic Institute and State University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ground based and jwst observations of sn 000000002022pul i unusual signatures of carbon oxygen and circumstellar interaction in a peculiar type ia supernova","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","ur