{"abstract":"This special issue is driven by a curiosity about the role of computational forms – practices, logics, technologies, and infrastructures – in social life and how they mediate issues of trust and mistrust: designated (mis)trust. Through a series of ethnographic encounters, its contributors describe how (mis)trust is rendered as an issue of concern by various actors as it is problematized, conceptualized, narrated, and designed for. In doing so, the papers analyse the work (mis)trust does in these settings, with a focus on the role of computational thinking within public discourses on democratic elections, the use of computational technologies in establishing bureaucratic order, the computational practices at play in the production of coding subjectivities, and the computational artefacts that assure data circulations within digital infrastructures. This introduction argues for a more expansive understanding of the relation between trust and mistrust in the digital age, countering the oftentimes default rendering of these concepts as antonymic. Instead, it argues that they live in a mutable relation. Despite prevailing technosolutionist approaches to (mis)trust, it cannot, we suggest, be solved for, resolved, or even eviscerated. Whatever actors (engineers, programmers, professionals etc) do in their efforts to ‘fix’ mistrust, it continues to mutate as a social form.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Maguire, James","Albris, Kristoffer"],"cuid":["S02-092.11-768534"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Computation","Digital","Mistrust","Mutations","Trust"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"digital mistrust ethnographic encounters with computational forms","src":["itu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/17530350.2024.2407853","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-092.11-768534","identifier":[{"id":"39610872","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85209661901","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC11601039","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["itu-35f1d3bd-525e-4799-89b6-27f23804b8b4","ku-ba9590be-9c04-4565-aa3d-c6f7e1c1943b"],"keyword":["Computation","Digital","Machinic","Mistrust","Mutations","Trust"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-C524207CA93348818B441C7340F4EE40"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/17530350.2024.2407853#abstract","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/17530350.2024.2407853","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Anthropology","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Anthropology, Copenhagen Center for Disaster Research","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Faculty of Social Sciences, shared expenditure, Social Data Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"James","key":"maguirepau","last":"Maguire","locid":"2efbc294-1ce4-4148-a403-93fe6450d879","name":"Maguire, James","orcid":"0000-0001-5081-1811","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Kristoffer Langkjær","key":"albrispau","last":"Albris","locid":"3562b196-6355-4e87-a1de-c22863765de9","name":"Albris, Kristoffer","name_org":"Albris, Kristoffer Langkjær","orcid":"0000-0002-1201-2231","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39610872"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/17530350.2024.2407853","issn":["17530350","17530369"],"issn_org":["17530350"],"issue":"6","journal":"Journal of Cultural Economy","pages":"725-736","publisher":"Routledge","status":"p","title":"Journal of Cultural Economy","volume":"17"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85209661901"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-35f1d3bd-525e-4799-89b6-27f23804b8b4","ku-ba9590be-9c04-4565-aa3d-c6f7e1c1943b"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Digital Mistrust : Ethnographic Encounters with Computational Forms","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-092.11-768534","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
