{"abstract":"Recently, electrically conducting heterointerfaces between dissimilar band insulators (such as lanthanum aluminate and strontium titanate) have attracted considerable research interest. Charge transport and fundamental aspects of conduction have been thoroughly explored. Perhaps surprisingly, similar studies on conceptually much simpler conducting homointerfaces, such as domain walls, are not nearly so well developed. Addressing this disparity, magnetoresistance is herein reported in approximately conical 180° charged domain walls, in partially switched ferroelectric thin-film single-crystal lithium niobate. This system is ideal for such measurements: first, the conductivity difference between domains and domain walls is unusually large (a factor of 1013) and hence currents driven through the thin film, between planar top and bottom electrodes, are overwhelmingly channeled along the walls; second, when electrical contact is made to the top and bottom of the domain walls and a magnetic field is applied along their cone axes, then the test geometry mirrors that of a Corbino disk: a textbook arrangement for geometric magnetoresistance measurement. Data imply carriers with extremely high room-temperature Hall mobilities of up to ≈3700 cm2 V−1 s−1. This is an unparalleled value for oxide interfaces (and for bulk oxides) comparable to mobilities in other systems seen at cryogenic, rather than at room, temperature.","author_count":15,"contributors":["McCluskey, Conor J.","Colbear, Matthew G.","McConville, James P. V.","McCartan, Shane J.","Maguire, Jesi R.","Conroy, Michele","Moore, Kalani","Harvey, Alan","Trier, Felix","Bangert, Ursel","Gruverman, Alexei","Bibes, Manuel","Kumar, Amit","McQuaid, Raymond G. P.","Gregg, J. Marty"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-379378"],"filters":{"added":"2022-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Gregg, J. Marty","McCluskey, Conor J."],"country":["France","Ireland","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Queen's University Belfast","University of Limerick","University of Nebraska-Lincoln","Université Paris-Saclay"],"keyword":["Carrier mobility","Domain walls","Ferroelectrics","Magnetoresistance"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ultra high carrier mobilities in ferroelectric domain wall corbino cones at room temperature","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/adma.202204298","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-379378","identifier":[{"id":"85133921095","type":"scopus"},{"id":"35733393","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-f9fb58ba-ae71-4283-af78-ae3c74e1ca32"],"keyword":["Carrier mobility","Corbino disks","Domain walls","Ferroelectrics","Magnetoresistance"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-760AB96E43FB938C9B30A36AECC1AF16"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/adma.202204298","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/283030197/Advanced_Materials_2022_McCluskey_Ultrahigh_Carrier_Mobilities_in_Ferroelectric_Domain_Wall_Corbino_Cones_at_Room_1_.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"queen s university belfast","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Queen's University Belfast","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ie","key":"university of limerick","loc":["Ireland","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Limerick","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Energy Conversion and Storage","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Energy Conversion and Storage, Functional Oxides"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"university of nebraska lincoln","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Nebraska-Lincoln","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"fr","key":"université paris saclay","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Université Paris-Saclay","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Conor J.","key":"mccluskeypau","last":"McCluskey","name":"McCluskey, Conor J.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Matthew G.","key":"colbearpau","last":"Colbear","name":"Colbear, Matthew G.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"James P. V.","key":"mcconvillepau","last":"McConville","name":"McConville, James P. V.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Shane J.","key":"mccartanpau","last":"McCartan","name":"McCartan, Shane J.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesi R.","key":"maguirepau","last":"Maguire","name":"Maguire, Jesi R.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Michele","key":"conroypau","last":"Conroy","name":"Conroy, Michele","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kalani","key":"moorepau","last":"Moore","name":"Moore, Kalani","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Alan","key":"harveypau","last":"Harvey","name":"Harvey, Alan","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Felix","key":"trierpau","last":"Trier","locid":"48b8db2c-2c79-49a3-bb19-490ca24652a6","name":"Trier, Felix","orcid":"0000-0003-0228-0635","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ursel","key":"bangertpau","last":"Bangert","name":"Bangert, Ursel","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Alexei","key":"gruvermanpau","last":"Gruverman","name":"Gruverman, Alexei","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Manuel","key":"bibespau","last":"Bibes","name":"Bibes, Manuel","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Amit","key":"kumarpau","last":"Kumar","name":"Kumar, Amit","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Raymond G. P.","key":"mcquaidpau","last":"McQuaid","name":"McQuaid, Raymond G. P.","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"J. Marty","key":"greggpau","last":"Gregg","name":"Gregg, J. Marty","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35733393"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/adma.202204298","issn":["09359648","09481907"],"issn_org":["09359648"],"issue":"32","journal":"Advanced Materials","paperid":"2204298","publisher":"Wiley-Blackwell","status":"p","title":"Advanced Materials","volume":"34"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85133921095"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-f9fb58ba-ae71-4283-af78-ae3c74e1ca32"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Ultra‐High Carrier Mobilities in Ferroelectric Domain Wall Corbino Cones at Room Temperature","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-379378","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background: Genetics and biology may influence the age of onset of anorexia nervosa (AN). The aims of this study were to determine whether common genetic variation contributes to age of onset of AN and to investigate the genetic associations between age of onset of AN and age at menarche. Methods: A secondary analysis of the Psychiatric Genomics Consortium genome-wide association study (GWAS) of AN was performed, which included 9335 cases and 31,981 screened controls, all from European ancestries. We conducted GWASs of age of onset, early-onset AN (<13 years), and typical-onset AN, and genetic correlation, genetic risk score, and Mendelian randomization analyses. Results: Two loci were genome-wide significant in the typical-onset AN GWAS. Heritability estimates (single nucleotide polymorphism–h2) were 0.01–0.04 for age of onset, 0.16–0.25 for early-onset AN, and 0.17–0.25 for typical-onset AN. Early- and typical-onset AN showed distinct genetic correlation patterns with putative risk factors for AN. Specifically, early-onset AN was significantly genetically correlated with younger age at menarche, and typical-onset AN was significantly negatively genetically correlated with anthropometric traits. Genetic risk scores for age of onset and early-onset AN estimated from independent GWASs significantly predicted age of onset. Mendelian randomization analysis suggested a causal link between younger age at menarche and early-onset AN. Conclusions: Our results provide evidence consistent with a common variant genetic basis for age of onset and implicate biological pathways regulating menarche and reproduction.","author_count":177,"contributors":["Watson, Hunna J.","Thornton, Laura M.","Yilmaz, Zeynep","Baker, Jessica H.","Coleman, Jonathan R.I.","Adan, Roger A.H.","Alfredsson, Lars","Andreassen, Ole A.","Ask, Helga","Berrettini, Wade H.","Boehnke, Michael","Boehm, Ilka","Boni, Claudette","Buehren, Katharina","Bulant, Josef","Burghardt, Roland","Chang, Xiao","Ci