{"abstract":"All of the contributions to this special issue are occupied with how to engage data otherwise. This otherwise indexes the rich variety of approaches to data beyond what we are currently witnessing. Whether through the development of politically and ethically relevant forms of data experiments, or the construction of alternative visions of the much-critiqued data infrastructures of powerful platform providers, all the articles reflect upon how we––as scholars and citizens––can live and work with data in ways amenable to diverse, critical, and ethical forms of social existence. This introduction intervenes in this debate in its own particular way, principally by considering what it means to characterise the contemporary as a data moment. The term data moment, we argue, works as a conceptual device calling for more ethical-political engagement with data practices. At the same time, it also retains a temporal inflection. Moments, we claim, are not sequential steps in a linear process, but are themselves productive of, and products of, temporal orders. Moments are also saturated in affect, we argue, and it is such affects that contribute to how particular forms of meaning emerge with/as data. By embracing the compelling empirical, theoretical and ethical challenges of this data moment our ambition with this special issue is to make a modest contribution to how scholars can engage data in the present, while also shaping a future where data are treated critically, ethically, and reflexively.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Maguire, James","Langstrup, Henriette","Danholt, Peter","Gad, Christopher"],"cuid":["S03-088.43-672845"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Maguire, James"],"keyword":["data moment temporality aesthetics narration qualitative quantitative experimental"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"engaging the data moment an introduction","src":["au","itu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85683152/Maguire_et_al_Engaging_the_data_moment.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-088.43-672845","ids":["au-f835debf-5cda-4e74-9870-1c4a0d76e594","itu-a35213f0-e196-47bf-91c6-612441b4fe48","ku-2e86e4db-9f32-44c9-ab7a-2555122bed39"],"keyword":["data moment, temporality, aesthetics, narration, qualitative-quantitative, experimental"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-3-2493277AB9FDAFAEBFE15AE0B65F6AE7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.dasts.dk/wp-content/uploads/1_introduction_FV_1.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85683152/Maguire_et_al_Engaging_the_data_moment.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.dasts.dk/?page_id=356","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Welfare","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Centre for Medical Science and Technology Studies","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Section of Health Services Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, School of Communication and Culture, School of Communication and Culture - Department of Digital Design and Information Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"James","key":"maguirepau","last":"Maguire","locid":"2efbc294-1ce4-4148-a403-93fe6450d879","name":"Maguire, James","orcid":"0000-0001-5081-1811","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Henriette","key":"langstruppau","last":"Langstrup","locid":"fc8cb988-7b7a-41be-b2c0-c5eb79f324b3","name":"Langstrup, Henriette","orcid":"0000-0002-3346-9396","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"danholtpau","last":"Danholt","locid":"eea95706-fae9-4f57-a925-428067bf259d","name":"Danholt, Peter","orcid":"0000-0002-4330-1239","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christopher","key":"gadpau","last":"Gad","locid":"d55dab65-fffe-4da4-a383-cfcf5ee3a8cd","name":"Gad, Christopher","orcid":"0000-0002-1631-5483","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["19044372"],"issue":"2","journal":"STS Encounters","pages":"1-21","paperid":"1","publisher":"Danish Association for Science and Technology Studies","status":"p","title":"STS Encounters","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Revi