{"abstract":"This paper offers an ethnographic perspective on the relationship between resource landscapes and the state in Iceland during a period of financial experimentation. In particular, it analyses a shift from the production of thermal water for local use to the production of electricity for the global aluminium market. This shift, the paper argues, is not merely a technocratic exercise in further resource extraction, it also indexes some of the tenuous connections between resource making and state making. The paper ends by offering a perspective on the recursive relationship between resource instabilities and instabilities within the state.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Maguire, James"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382308"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["capital energy earthquakes landscapes resources the state Iceland"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"icelandic resource landscapes and the state experiments in energy capital and aluminium","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3167/ajec.2020.290103","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382308","identifier":[{"id":"85087715923","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-45fb9bf6-3fa8-4ced-babe-c8dcbef741cb"],"keyword":["capital; energy; earthquakes; landscapes; resources; the state; Iceland"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-CAD8C811EE5B4894251462A49154902E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3167/ajec.2020.290103","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85579419/Maguire_Icelandic_Resource_Landscapes_and_the_State.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Welfare","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"James","key":"maguirepau","last":"Maguire","locid":"2efbc294-1ce4-4148-a403-93fe6450d879","name":"Maguire, James","orcid":"0000-0001-5081-1811","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3167/ajec.2020.290103","issn":["17552923","17552931"],"issn_org":["17552923"],"issue":"1","journal":"Anthropological Journal of European Cultures","pages":"20-41","paperid":"3","publisher":"Berghahn Books","status":"p","title":"Anthropological Journal of European Cultures","volume":"29"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85087715923"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-45fb9bf6-3fa8-4ced-babe-c8dcbef741cb"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Icelandic Resource Landscapes and the State : Experiments in Energy, Capital, and Aluminium","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382308","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
