{"abstract":"Edge infrastructures–– as a newly emerging computing paradigm––are one form of industry response to the need to diversify our digital infrastructures. While not replacing centralized digital processes, edge is one way, this report argues, to facilitate a transition to more decentralised arrangements. The report gives an overview of the expectations and promises of edge. Focusing on SMEs, the report also identifies five areas of opportunity for edge impleme ntation: the effects of the Covid-19 pandemic, advances in manufacturing andhealthcare, future retail needs, and smart city developments.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Maguire, James","Canureci, Cristina-Elena"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383661"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["edge infratsructure emerging technologies digital transitions"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"emerging technologies the case of edge computing","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85589011/Emerging_Technologies_Edge_Computing.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383661","ids":["itu-a4029e9b-f5f8-427a-8976-4dbee9cc2ce2"],"keyword":["edge, infratsructure, emerging technologies, digital transitions"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-A534D087C854B49CCBB7677A2BD98B86"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85589011/Emerging_Technologies_Edge_Computing.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Welfare","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"James","key":"maguirepau","last":"Maguire","locid":"2efbc294-1ce4-4148-a403-93fe6450d879","name":"Maguire, James","orcid":"0000-0001-5081-1811","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Cristina-Elena","key":"canurecipau","last":"Canureci","name":"Canureci, Cristina-Elena","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"17","publisher":"IT-Universitetet i København","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-a4029e9b-f5f8-427a-8976-4dbee9cc2ce2"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Emerging Technologies : The case of Edge Computing","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383661","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Big-Tech’s data centres have recently emerged as important socio-political figures in the ongoing digitalisation of the Danish state. Locating vast swathes of data in a country renowned for its renewable energy has prompted a series of questions about the nature of the relationship between these two actors. Our ethnographic interest resides in analysing how, and why, Denmark is rapidly becoming Europe’s primary US data centre location, and in exploring the transformative processes through which the Danish state is being reconfigured as digital. In doing so, we emphasise the role of infrastructures in digital state-making and draw upon a particular reading of anthropological exchange theory to conceptualise how the state is being reconstituted through exchange practices with data centre actors. We argue that as Big-Tech territorialises state land and resources, the state in turn reterritorializes the promising digital futures that come with Big-Tech, making visible its new digital frontier.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Maguire, James","Winthereik, Brit Ross"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381274"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["data centres digitalisation Big Tech the state energy infrastructure"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"digitalising the state data centres and the power of exchange","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84065653/Maguire_Winthereik_Digitalizing_the_State_copy.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-381274","identifier":[{"id":"85071984248","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-018590c2-e7a5-4026-978c-92e9e5828ffd"],"keyword":["data centres, digitalisation, Big-Tech, the state, energy, infrastructure"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3C9866CC8C521DB2A8925D172A01CC4D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84065653/Maguire_Winthereik_Digitalizing_the_State_copy.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"James","key":"maguirepau","last":"Maguire","locid":"2efbc294-1ce4-4148-a403-93fe6450d879","name":"Maguire, James","orcid":"0000-0001-5081-1811","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Brit Ross","key":"winthereikpau","last":"Winthereik","name":"Winthereik, Brit Ross","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/00141844.2019.1660391","issn":["00141844","1469588X"],"issn_org":["00141844"],"journal":"Ethnos","publisher":"Routledge","status":"p","title":"Ethnos"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85071984248"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-018590c2-e7a5-4026-978c-92e9e5828ffd"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Digitalising the State : Data Centres and the Power of Exchange","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381274","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Background: Epigenetic mechanisms, including methylation, can contribute to childhood asthma. Identifying DNA methylation profiles in asthmatic patients can inform disease pathogenesis. Objective: We sought to identify differential DNA methylation in newborns and children related to childhood asthma. Methods: Within the Pregnancy And Childhood Epigenetics consortium, we performed epigenome-wide meta-analyses of school-age asthma in relation to CpG methylation (Illumina450K) in blood measured either in newborns, in prospective analyses, or cross-sectionally in school-aged children. We also identified differentially methylated regions. Results: In newborns (8 cohorts, 668 cases), 9 CpGs (and 35 regions) were differentially methylated (epigenome-wide significance, false discovery rate < 0.05) in relation to asthma development. In a cross-sectional meta-analysis of asthma and methylation in children (9 cohorts, 631 cases), we identified 179 CpGs (false discovery rate < 0.05) and 36 differentially methylated regions. In replication studies of methylation in other tissues, most of the 179 CpGs discovered in blood replicated, despite smaller sample sizes, in studies of nasal respiratory epithelium or eosinophils. Pathway analyses highlighted enrichment for asthma-relevant immune processes and overlap in pathways enriched both in newborns and children. Gene expression correlated with methylation at most loci. Functional annotation supports a regulatory effect on gene expression at many asthma-associated CpGs. Several implicated genes are targets for approved or experimental drugs, including IL5RA and KCNH2. Conclusion: Novel loci differentially methylated in newborns represent potential biomarkers of risk of asthma by school age. Cross-sectional associations in children can reflect both risk for and effects of disease. Asthma-related differential methylation in blood in children was substantially replicated in eosinophils and respiratory epithelium.","author_count":50,"contributors":["Reese, Sarah E","Xu, Cheng-Jian","den Dekker, Herman T","Lee, Mi Kyeong","Sikdar, Sinjini","Ruiz-Arenas, Carlos","Merid, Simon K","Rezwan, Faisal I","Page, Christian M","Ullemar, Vilhelmina","Melton, Phillip E","Oh, Sam S","Yang, Ivana V","Burrows, Kimberley","Söderhäll, Cilla","Jima, Dereje D","Gao, Lu","Arathimos, Ryan","Küpers, Leanne K","Wielscher, Matthias","Rzehak, Peter","Lahti, Jari","Laprise, Catherine","Madore, Anne-Marie","Ward, James","Bennett, Brian D","Wang, Tianyuan","Bell, Douglas A","Vonk, Judith M","Håberg, Siri E","Zhao, Shanshan","Karlsson, Robert","Hollams, Elysia","Hu, Donglei","Richards, Adam J","Bergström, Anna","Sharp, Gemma C","Felix, Janine F","Bustamante, Mariona","Gruzieva, Olena","Maguire, Rachel L","Gilliland, Frank","Baïz, Nour","Nohr, Ellen A","Corpeleijn, Eva","Sebert, Sylvain","Karmaus, Wilfried","Grote, Veit","Kajantie, Eero","Magnus, Maria C"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-632282"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"corpau":["BIOS Consortium"],"country":["Australia","Finland","Germany","Netherlands","Norway","Spain","Sweden","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Barcelona Institute of Science and Technology","CIBER Epidemiologia Y Salud Publica","Curtin University","Duke University Medical Center","Erasmus University Medical Center Rotterdam","Helsinki University Hospital","Imperial College London","Karolinska Institute","Ludwig-Maximilian University of Munich","National Institute of Environmental Health Sciences","North Carolina State University","Norwegian Institute of Public Health","Oslo University Hospital","Pompeu Fabra University","Stockholm County Council, Stockholm, Sweden","The University of Western Australia","University Medical Center Groningen","University of Bristol","University of California, San Francisco","University of Colorado Denver Anschutz Medical Campus","University of Groningen","University of Helsinki","University of Memphis","University of Oulu","University of Southampton","University of Southern California"],"keyword":["Asthma","Childhood","Drug development","Epigenetics","Methylation","Newborn"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Centre intégré universitaire de santé et de services sociaux du Saguenay, Saguenay, Quebec, Canada; Département des sciences fondamentales, Université du Québec à Chicoutimi, Saguenay, Quebec, Canada."],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"epigenome wide meta analysis of dna methylation and childhood asthma","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jaci.2018.11.043","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-632282","identifier":[{"id":"30579849","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85060282097","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC6556405","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["sdu-ce2565e3-701f-458a-953c-5b1ba9a1275a"],"keyword":["Epigenetics","asthma","childhood","drug development","methylation","newborn"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-CA1404C4DF672805EAD6BD4121B8FCAF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/151402186/Epigenome_wide_Meta_analysis_of_DNA_Methylation_and_Childhood_Asthma.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jaci.2018.11.043","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"national institute of environmental health sciences","loc":["United States","America, North","OEC