avis","University of California, Davis","University of Cambridge","University of Cape Town","University of Cologne","University of Erlangen-Nuremberg, Germany","University of Florence","University of Freiburg","University of Glasgow","University of Gothenburg","University of Greifswald","University of Göttingen","University of Hamburg","University of Lausanne","University of Leicester","University of Lisbon","University of Luxembourg","University of Lübeck","University of Manitoba","University of Marburg","University of Massachusetts Medical School","University of Melbourne","University of Michigan","University of Michigan, Ann Arbor","University of Milan","University of Milan - Bicocca","University of Milano-Bicocca","University of Minnesota","University of Minnesota Twin Cities","University of Modena and Reggio Emilia","University of Naples Federico II","University of Oxford","University of Palermo","University of Pennsylvania","University of Regensburg","University of Rijeka","University of Rochester","University of Rochester Medical Center","University of Rome La Sapienza","University of Salamanca","University of Siena","University of Sydney","University of São Paulo","University of Tartu","University of Technology Sydney","University of Texas MD Anderson Cancer Center","University of Toronto","University of Udine","University of Valencia","University of Verona","University of Veterinary Medicine Vienna","University of Zurich","University of Zürich","Université Paris Cité","Université catholique de Louvain","Utrecht University","Washington University St. Louis","Washington University in St. Louis","West China Hospital of Sichuan University","Westmead Institute for Medical Research","Westmead Millennium Institute for Medical Research","Wuhan University","Yeshiva University","Yong Loo Lin School of Medicine"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Institut für Transfusionsmedizin, Universitätsklinik Schleswig-Holstein, Kiel, Germany."],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"guidelines for the use of flow cytometry and cell sorting in immunological studies second edition","src":["dtu","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"http://europepmc.org/Copyright","type":"rem","url":"http://europepmc.org/articles/pmc7350392?pdf=render","version":"Authors Final Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Ramon Bellmàs Sanz, Jenny Kühne, and Christine S. Falk thank Jana Keil and Kerstin Daemen for excellent technical support. The work was funded by the Germany Research Foundation CRC738/B3 (CSF). Larissa Nogueira Almeida was supported by DFG research grant MA 2273/14‐1. Rudolf A. Manz was supported by the Excellence Cluster “Inflammation at Interfaces” (EXC 306/2). Susanne Hartmann and Friederike Ebner were supported by the German Research Foundation (GRK 2046). Edwin van der Pol and Paola Lanuti acknowledge Aleksandra Gąsecka M.D. for excellent experimental support and Dr. Rienk Nieuwland for textual suggestions. This work was supported by the Netherlands Organisation for Scientific Research – Domain Applied and Engineering Sciences (NWO‐TTW), research program VENI 15924. Hans Minderman was supported by NIH R50CA211108. Work in the laboratory of Dieter Adam is supported by the Deutsche Forschungsgemeinschaft (DFG, German Research Foundation)—Projektnummer 125440785 – SFB 877, Project B2. Christian Kukat acknowledges support from the ISAC SRL Emerging Leaders program. This work was funded by the Deutsche Forschungsgemeinschaft through the grant TRR130 (project P11 and C03) to Thomas H. Winkler. The Immunology Database and Analysis Portal (ImmPort) system provides an archive of immunology research data generated by investigators mainly funded through the National Institutes of Health (NIH), National Institute of Allergy and Infectious Diseases (NIAID), and Division of Allergy, Immunology, and Transplantation (DAIT). It is an extensive data warehouse containing an integration of experimental and clinical trial data generated by dozens of assay types, including 131 FCM and 24 CyTOF data sets. In addition, the ImmPort system also provides data analysis tools and it contains implicit knowledge and ‘‘best practices’’ for clinical and genomic studies in the form of ∼50 templates for data deposition, management, and dissemination. ImmPort has been developed under the Bioinformatics Integration Support Contract (BISC) by the Northrop Grumman Information Technology Health Solutions team for the NIH NIAID/DAIT. If your research funding comes from this source and you are generating immunology data, you should deposit it in ImmPort. Immport's support for different data types can be another reason to choose it if you are generating FCM data as well as data from different types of assays. A (free) registration and approval by DAIT is required in order to deposit and access data from ImmPort. A potential drawback of using this resource is that there can be a long delay in publication of deposited datasets. The work by the Mei laboratory was supported by German Research Foundation Grant ME 3644/5‐1 and TRR130 TP24, the German Rheumatism Research Centre Berlin, European Union Innovative Medicines Initiative ‐ Joint Undertaking ‐ RTCure Grant Agreement 777357, the Else Kröner‐Fresenius‐Foundation, German Federal Ministry of Education and Research e:Med sysINFLAME Program Grant 01ZX1306B and KMU‐innovativ “InnoCyt”, and the Leibniz Science Campus for Chronic Inflammation ( http://www.chronische-entzuendung.org ). Petra Hoffmann, Andrea Hauser, and Matthias Edinger thank BD Biosciences®, San José, CA, USA, and SKAN AG, Bale, Switzerland for fruitful cooperation during the development, construction, and installation of the GMP‐compliant cell sorting equipment and the Bavarian Immune Therapy Network (BayImmuNet) for financial support. John Trowsdale received funding from the European Research Council under the European Union's Horizon 2020 research and innovation program (Grant Agreement 695551)."],"id":"S03-095.40-035982","identifier":[{"id":"000491166500003","type":"wos"},{"id":"85073598520","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC7350392","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"31633216","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-94921408-d4c2-405d-94c9-22ee4e4bcb29","ku-9e37d85d-e5a6-4d24-ac2c-5efcd72b831f","sdu-3fcd4576-74a2-44c8-a75a-32906b960113"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-3AFD14C83119C274A85AB3C2313CB38D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"http://europepmc.org/Copyright","type":"rem","url":"http://europepmc.org/articles/pmc7350392?pdf=render","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"it","key":"university of modena and reggio emilia","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Modena and Reggio Emilia","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"humboldt university of berlin","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Humboldt University of Berlin","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"friedrich alexander university erlangen nürnberg","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Friedrich-Alexander University Erlangen-Nürnberg","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"de","key":"university of erlangen nuremberg germany","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Erlangen-Nuremberg, Germany","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"de","key":"kiel university","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Kiel University","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"de","key":"christian albrechts university of kiel","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Christian-Albrechts-University of Kiel","used":1},{"affno":"7","key"